From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:19:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the frame cache's tracked state across a replay

- Replaying a square rectangle binds texture 0 through Renderer's own
  functions, which wrote the state the recording tracks; replayed binds
  did not. The next frame then started from another state than the one
  kept with the frame on screen and was drawn again though nothing
  changed (about two idle frames in three on a view with one). The
  tracked state is saved and put back around each replay.
---
 es-core/src/renderers/Renderer.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/es-core/src/renderers/Renderer.cpp b/es-core/src/renderers/Renderer.cpp
index f71b1d2d..c16c41b6 100644
--- a/es-core/src/renderers/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/renderers/Renderer.cpp
@@ -1027,6 +1027,11 @@ namespace Renderer
 			bool wasRecording = recording;
 			recording = false;
 
+			// The state the recording tracks stays the recording's: a replayed square rectangle binds texture 0
+			// through Renderer's own functions, and the next frame would start from another state than the one
+			// kept with the frame on screen (it would never compare equal)
+			State tracked = state;
+
 			for (; sent < frame.commands.size(); sent++)
 			{
 				const Command& c = frame.commands[sent];
@@ -1049,6 +1054,7 @@ namespace Renderer
 				}
 			}
 
+			state = tracked;
 			recording = wasRecording;
 		}
 
